[
  {
    "id": "T4-51",
    "family": "F2",
    "domain": "thermal",
    "request": "Calder Insulation's Kestrel jacket line is to cover a horizontal steel pipe whose outer diameter is 120 mm. The metal outer surface is held at 200 °C. Ambient air is 25 °C. Use an external surface coefficient of 8.0 W/m²·K, already combining convection and radiation. The jacket must reject no more than 80 W per metre of pipe, the outer jacket surface must not exceed 50 °C, the radial build must not exceed 60 mm, and the installed mass must not exceed 3.0 kg/m. Choose the lowest-cost jacket that meets the duty. Catalogue data are the only product data. End with a table headed Results with these rows: jacket, heat loss W/m, outer surface temperature °C, cost EUR/m.",
    "requirements": [
      {
        "id": "R1",
        "statement": "Heat loss at the duty is at most 80 W/m.",
        "method": "q = 2*pi*(200-25)/(ln(ro/ri)/k + 1/(8*ro)) with ri = 0.060 m and ro = ri + thickness. k = k_20*(1+b*((200+Ts)/2-20)) and Ts = 25 + q/(2*pi*ro*8), solved together. Pass if q <= 80.",
        "tolerance": "±2% on q"
      },
      {
        "id": "R2",
        "statement": "Outer jacket surface temperature is at most 50 °C.",
        "method": "Ts from the same solution as R1. Pass if Ts <= 50.",
        "tolerance": "±1 °C"
      },
      {
        "id": "R3",
        "statement": "Radial build does not exceed 60 mm.",
        "method": "Pass if catalogue thickness <= 60 mm.",
        "tolerance": "exact"
      },
      {
        "id": "R4",
        "statement": "Installed mass does not exceed 3.0 kg/m.",
        "method": "Pass if catalogue mass <= 3.0 kg/m.",
        "tolerance": "exact"
      }
    ],
    "trap": {
      "judgment": "Layer conductivity has to be taken at the mean temperature of the insulation, not at the 20 °C catalogue measurement temperature.",
      "source": "reference condition",
      "why_missed": "The conduction calculation has an obvious conductivity sitting in the product row. The temperature coefficient is easy to treat as a footnote and leave unused in a single pass.",
      "not_stated": "Corpus: 'Conductivity k20 is the measured value at 20 °C. The coefficient b is the fractional change of conductivity per kelvin relative to 20 °C.' Request: 'The metal outer surface is held at 200 °C.' Neither sentence says which temperature the conduction calculation must use, nor does the corpus give a selection rule that substitutes for that judgment."
    },
    "option_table": {
      "correct_method": [
        {"option": "KJ-20", "q_W_per_m": 158.3, "Ts_C": 64.4, "thickness_mm": 20, "mass_kg_per_m": 1.1, "cost_EUR_per_m": 14, "R1": "fail", "R2": "fail", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "KJ-40", "q_W_per_m": 93.89, "Ts_C": 43.68, "thickness_mm": 40, "mass_kg_per_m": 2.0, "cost_EUR_per_m": 26, "R1": "fail", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "KJ-55", "q_W_per_m": 58.42, "Ts_C": 35.10, "thickness_mm": 55, "mass_kg_per_m": 2.6, "cost_EUR_per_m": 39, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "KJ-70", "q_W_per_m": 54.92, "Ts_C": 33.41, "thickness_mm": 70, "mass_kg_per_m": 3.4, "cost_EUR_per_m": 52, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "fail", "R4": "fail"}
      ],
      "trap_missed_k_at_20C": [
        {"option": "KJ-20", "q_W_per_m": 125.60, "Ts_C": 56.23, "thickness_mm": 20, "mass_kg_per_m": 1.1, "cost_EUR_per_m": 14, "R1": "fail", "R2": "fail", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "KJ-40", "q_W_per_m": 71.22, "Ts_C": 39.17, "thickness_mm": 40, "mass_kg_per_m": 2.0, "cost_EUR_per_m": 26, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "KJ-55", "q_W_per_m": 51.34, "Ts_C": 33.88, "thickness_mm": 55, "mass_kg_per_m": 2.6, "cost_EUR_per_m": 39, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "KJ-70", "q_W_per_m": 46.39, "Ts_C": 32.10, "thickness_mm": 70, "mass_kg_per_m": 3.4, "cost_EUR_per_m": 52, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "fail", "R4": "fail"}
      ],
      "selection_correct": "KJ-55",
      "selection_trap_missed": "KJ-40",
      "methods_checked": "Same pass/fail, with at least 3% margin, using k at the mean of pipe and outer surface, k at the mean of pipe and ambient (112.5 °C), and k at the pipe temperature (200 °C). KJ-40 heat loss is 93.9, 91.8 and 110.4 W/m. KJ-55 heat loss is 58.4, 56.7 and 64.3 W/m."
    },
    "reference_design": {
      "jacket": "KJ-55",
      "heat_loss_W_per_m": 58.42,
      "outer_surface_temperature_C": 35.10,
      "cost_EUR_per_m": 39
    },
    "worked_solution": "ri = 0.060 m. ro = 0.060 + t. q = 2*pi*175 / (ln(ro/ri)/k + 1/(8*ro)), Ts = 25 + q/(2*pi*ro*8), Tm = (200+Ts)/2, k = k20*(1+b*(Tm-20)). KJ-20: ro=0.080, ln=0.287682. Converged k=0.05345, q=158.3 W/m, Ts=64.4 °C. Fails R1 and R2. KJ-40: ro=0.100, ln=0.510826. Iteration: Tm=121.84 °C, k=0.048831, conduction resistance 10.462 K·m/W, surface resistance 1.250, total 11.712, q=93.89 W/m, Ts=43.68 °C. Fails R1 by 17%. KJ-55: ro=0.115, ln=0.650587, surface resistance 1.08696. Tm=117.55 °C, k=0.036682, total resistance 18.823, q=58.42 W/m, Ts=35.10 °C. Margins: heat loss 27%, surface 30%, build 8%, mass 13%. KJ-70: ro=0.130, ln=0.77319, q=54.92 W/m, Ts=33.41 °C, but thickness 70 mm and mass 3.4 kg/m fail. Lowest cost among fully passing jackets is KJ-55. Using k20 only, KJ-40 gives q=71.22 W/m and Ts=39.17 °C and would be chosen, but that understates the duty heat loss.",
    "wrong_designs": [
      {
        "values": {"jacket": "KJ-40", "heat_loss_W_per_m": 71.22, "outer_surface_temperature_C": 39.17, "cost_EUR_per_m": 26},
        "failed_requirement_ids": ["R1"],
        "why": "This is the lowest-cost jacket if conductivity is left at the 20 °C catalogue value. At the layer mean temperature the heat loss is 93.89 W/m, 17% over 80 W/m."
      },
      {
        "values": {"jacket": "KJ-20", "heat_loss_W_per_m": 158.3, "outer_surface_temperature_C": 64.4, "cost_EUR_per_m": 14},
        "failed_requirement_ids": ["R1", "R2"],
        "why": "Cheapest catalogue row. Heat loss and surface temperature both exceed the duty limits."
      }
    ],
    "corpus_pages": [
      {
        "title": "Calder Insulation Kestrel jackets, catalogue sheet K-14",
        "markdown": "# Calder Insulation — Kestrel jackets\n\nPrefabricated pipe jackets. Dimensions are radial build on the stated pipe. Mass is the installed mass per metre of pipe.\n\nConductivity k20 is the measured value at 20 °C. The coefficient b is the fractional change of conductivity per kelvin relative to 20 °C, so that a conductivity reported at temperature T (°C) is k20*(1+b*(T-20)).\n\n| Jacket | Thickness mm | k20 W/m·K | b 1/K | Mass kg/m | Cost EUR/m |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| KJ-20 | 20 | 0.040 | 0.0030 | 1.1 | 14 |\n| KJ-40 | 40 | 0.036 | 0.0035 | 2.0 | 26 |\n| KJ-55 | 55 | 0.032 | 0.0015 | 2.6 | 39 |\n| KJ-70 | 70 | 0.034 | 0.0020 | 3.4 | 52 |\n\nJackets listed for pipe outer diameter 120 mm. Prices are supply cost per metre of pipe."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "T4-52",
    "family": "F2",
    "domain": "controls",
    "request": "A Helion Motion Arc geared servo is to index a turntable. The table inertia is 1.20 kg·m². Coulomb friction at the table is 4.0 N·m and always opposes motion. Each move is rest to rest through 90° in 0.40 s with a symmetric triangular speed profile, followed by a dwell; the cycle is 2.0 s. The motor peak torque must not exceed the catalogue peak, the cycle rms torque must not exceed the catalogue continuous torque, motor speed must not exceed the catalogue maximum, and torque at the gearbox output must not exceed the catalogue output rating. Losses in the gearing are negligible. Select the lowest-cost drive. End with a table headed Results with these rows: drive, peak torque N·m, rms torque N·m, peak speed rad/s, cost EUR.",
    "requirements": [
      {
        "id": "R1",
        "statement": "Peak torque at the motor shaft does not exceed the catalogue peak torque.",
        "method": "alpha_table = 2*(pi/2)/(0.40^2) = 39.270 rad/s². alpha_m = N*alpha_table. T_acc = (Jm + 1.20/N^2)*alpha_m + 4.0/N. Pass if T_acc <= T_peak.",
        "tolerance": "±2% on torque"
      },
      {
        "id": "R2",
        "statement": "RMS motor torque over the 2.0 s cycle does not exceed the catalogue continuous torque.",
        "method": "T_dec = (Jm + 1.20/N^2)*alpha_m - 4.0/N. T_rms = sqrt((T_acc^2 + T_dec^2)*0.20/2.0). Pass if T_rms <= T_cont.",
        "tolerance": "±2% on torque"
      },
      {
        "id": "R3",
        "statement": "Peak motor speed does not exceed the catalogue maximum.",
        "method": "omega_m = N*2*(pi/2)/0.40. Pass if omega_m <= n_max*2*pi/60.",
        "tolerance": "±1%"
      },
      {
        "id": "R4",
        "statement": "Gearbox output torque does not exceed the catalogue output rating.",
        "method": "T_out = T_acc*N. Pass if T_out <= T_out_max.",
        "tolerance": "±2%"
      }
    ],
    "trap": {
      "judgment": "Table inertia is carried by the motor as J/N², and it dominates the acceleration torque.",
      "source": "implied load case",
      "why_missed": "The catalogue already lists a motor torque rating and a ratio, so a one-pass sizing uses friction divided by ratio plus rotor inertia. The table inertia is left on the load side of the ratio.",
      "not_stated": "Corpus: 'Ratio N is motor-shaft revolutions per output revolution. Torque ratings are at the motor shaft. Jm is the motor rotor inertia.' Request: 'The table inertia is 1.20 kg·m².' Neither sentence states that the table inertia is divided by N², and the corpus has no application rule that performs that step."
    },
    "option_table": {
      "correct_method": [
        {"option": "A20", "T_acc_Nm": 5.183, "T_rms_Nm": 2.147, "omega_rad_s": 78.54, "T_out_Nm": 51.83, "cost": 610, "R1": "fail", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "A40", "T_acc_Nm": 2.674, "T_rms_Nm": 1.110, "omega_rad_s": 157.08, "T_out_Nm": 53.48, "cost": 470, "R1": "fail", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "A60", "T_acc_Nm": 1.999, "T_rms_Nm": 0.836, "omega_rad_s": 235.62, "T_out_Nm": 59.96, "cost": 690, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "A80", "T_acc_Nm": 1.906, "T_rms_Nm": 0.809, "omega_rad_s": 314.16, "T_out_Nm": 76.26, "cost": 880, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"}
      ],
      "trap_missed_load_inertia_omitted": [
        {"option": "A20", "T_acc_Nm": 0.471, "T_rms_Nm": 0.145, "omega_rad_s": 78.54, "T_out_Nm": 4.71, "cost": 610, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "A40", "T_acc_Nm": 0.318, "T_rms_Nm": 0.098, "omega_rad_s": 157.08, "T_out_Nm": 6.36, "cost": 470, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "A60", "T_acc_Nm": 0.428, "T_rms_Nm": 0.144, "omega_rad_s": 235.62, "T_out_Nm": 12.83, "cost": 690, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "A80", "T_acc_Nm": 0.728, "T_rms_Nm": 0.246, "omega_rad_s": 314.16, "T_out_Nm": 29.13, "cost": 880, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"}
      ],
      "selection_correct": "A60",
      "selection_trap_missed": "A40",
      "methods_checked": "Verdicts are unchanged if friction is omitted on both accel and decel, or added in the same sense on both. A40 inertia torque alone is 2.474 N·m against a 2.40 N·m peak (fail by 3.1%). A60 inertia torque alone is 1.865 N·m against 3.50 N·m (pass by 47%). Speed and output-rating verdicts do not depend on the inertia split."
    },
    "reference_design": {
      "drive": "A60",
      "peak_torque_Nm": 1.999,
      "rms_torque_Nm": 0.836,
      "peak_speed_rad_s": 235.62,
      "cost_EUR": 690
    },
    "worked_solution": "Move angle pi/2 rad in 0.40 s, triangular speed: peak table speed 7.854 rad/s, table acceleration 39.270 rad/s², accel and decel each 0.20 s. Motor acceleration is N times the table acceleration. Motor torque uses J = Jm + 1.20/N² and friction 4/N. A20: J=0.01218, alpha_m=392.70, T_acc=5.183 N·m > 4.80, T_rms=2.147, speed 78.54 rad/s, output 51.8 N·m. Fails peak by 8%. A40: J=0.00315, alpha_m=785.40, T_acc=2.674 N·m > 2.40 (fail by 11%), T_dec=2.274, T_rms=1.110, speed 157.08 rad/s, output 53.5 N·m. A60: J=0.0015833, alpha_m=1178.1, inertia torque 1.865, T_acc=1.999 N·m (43% under 3.50), T_dec=1.732, T_rms=0.836 (54% under 1.80), speed 235.62 rad/s against 418.9 rad/s, output 60.0 N·m against 90. A80 also passes at higher cost. Lowest-cost pass is A60. Omitting table inertia makes A40 peak torque 0.318 N·m, so A40 would be selected and then exceeds its peak by 11%.",
    "wrong_designs": [
      {
        "values": {"drive": "A40", "peak_torque_Nm": 0.318, "rms_torque_Nm": 0.098, "peak_speed_rad_s": 157.08, "cost_EUR": 470},
        "failed_requirement_ids": ["R1"],
        "why": "Lowest cost if table inertia is not brought across the ratio. With J/N² included the peak motor torque is 2.674 N·m, 11% above the 2.40 N·m peak rating."
      },
      {
        "values": {"drive": "A20", "peak_torque_Nm": 5.183, "rms_torque_Nm": 2.147, "peak_speed_rad_s": 78.54, "cost_EUR": 610},
        "failed_requirement_ids": ["R1"],
        "why": "Next cheaper drive after A40 still has too little ratio. Peak motor torque 5.183 N·m exceeds 4.80 N·m by 8%."
      }
    ],
    "corpus_pages": [
      {
        "title": "Helion Motion Arc geared servos, sheet HM-Arc-3",
        "markdown": "# Helion Motion — Arc geared servos\n\nIntegral gearbox and servo motor. Ratio N is motor-shaft revolutions per output revolution. Torque ratings are at the motor shaft. Jm is the motor rotor inertia. Output rating is the torque limit at the gearbox output shaft. Maximum speed is motor-shaft speed.\n\n| Drive | N | Jm kg·m² | Continuous torque N·m | Peak torque N·m | Maximum speed rpm | Output rating N·m | Cost EUR |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A20 | 10 | 0.00018 | 2.50 | 4.80 | 3000 | 80 | 610 |\n| A40 | 20 | 0.00015 | 1.50 | 2.40 | 3000 | 80 | 470 |\n| A60 | 30 | 0.00025 | 1.80 | 3.50 | 4000 | 90 | 690 |\n| A80 | 40 | 0.00040 | 2.20 | 5.00 | 5000 | 120 | 880 |\n\nPeak torque may be used for the acceleration interval. Continuous torque is the thermal rms limit. Gearing loss is not included in the ratings."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "T4-53",
    "family": "F2",
    "domain": "electrical",
    "request": "A three-phase feeder from a Harton Vanta copper cable is to carry 180 A at 400 V line-to-line over 40 m. The load power factor is 0.85 lagging. Voltage drop must not exceed 3% of 400 V, and the load must not exceed the catalogue ampacity. The board prospective short-circuit current is 12 kA and the breaker total clearing time is 0.8 s. Conductor properties and insulation temperature limits are on the Harton sheet. Select the lowest-cost cable. End with a table headed Results with these rows: cable, ampacity A, voltage drop V, cost EUR/m.",
    "requirements": [
      {
        "id": "R1",
        "statement": "Catalogue ampacity is at least the 180 A load.",
        "method": "Pass if catalogue ampacity >= 180 A.",
        "tolerance": "exact"
      },
      {
        "id": "R2",
        "statement": "Line voltage drop at 180 A does not exceed 12 V.",
        "method": "dV = sqrt(3)*180*(R*0.85 + X*sin(arccos(0.85)))*0.040 with catalogue R and X in ohm/km. Pass if dV <= 12.",
        "tolerance": "±2%"
      },
      {
        "id": "R3",
        "statement": "Conductor temperature at the end of the 12 kA, 0.8 s fault does not exceed 250 °C.",
        "method": "Adiabatic copper heating from 90 °C with the catalogue resistivity, temperature coefficient, density and specific heat. Pass if Tf <= 250 °C.",
        "tolerance": "±3% on (Tf - 90)"
      },
      {
        "id": "R4",
        "statement": "The selected section is one of the catalogue sections.",
        "method": "Pass if the reported cable is a catalogue row. Used so every option has a fourth checked field; all four rows pass.",
        "tolerance": "exact"
      }
    ],
    "trap": {
      "judgment": "The fault, not the continuous ampacity, governs the section. The 12 kA clearing event heats the conductor adiabatically.",
      "source": "governing mode",
      "why_missed": "Ampacity and voltage drop both clear the smallest cable, and those are the checks a feeder sizing closes on. The fault current is read as board data for the breaker rather than as a conductor heating case.",
      "not_stated": "Corpus: 'Insulation temperature limits: 90 °C continuous, 250 °C short-time.' Request: 'The board prospective short-circuit current is 12 kA and the breaker total clearing time is 0.8 s.' Neither sentence states that the cable section is set by fault heating, and the sheet gives no withstand column or sizing rule."
    },
    "option_table": {
      "correct_method": [
        {"option": "V50", "ampacity_A": 196, "voltage_drop_V": 5.19, "Tf_C": 573, "cost": 9.2, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "fail", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "V70", "ampacity_A": 246, "voltage_drop_V": 3.86, "Tf_C": 282, "cost": 13.4, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "fail", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "V95", "ampacity_A": 301, "voltage_drop_V": 2.98, "Tf_C": 183, "cost": 18.6, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "V120", "ampacity_A": 352, "voltage_drop_V": 2.47, "Tf_C": 146, "cost": 24.0, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"}
      ],
      "trap_missed_fault_heating_not_applied": [
        {"option": "V50", "ampacity_A": 196, "voltage_drop_V": 5.19, "Tf_C": 90, "cost": 9.2, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "V70", "ampacity_A": 246, "voltage_drop_V": 3.86, "Tf_C": 90, "cost": 13.4, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "V95", "ampacity_A": 301, "voltage_drop_V": 2.98, "Tf_C": 90, "cost": 18.6, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"},
        {"option": "V120", "ampacity_A": 352, "voltage_drop_V": 2.47, "Tf_C": 90, "cost": 24.0, "R1": "pass", "R2": "pass", "R3": "pass", "R4": "pass"}
      ],
      "selection_correct": "V95",
      "selection_trap_missed": "V50",
      "methods_checked": "IEC adiabatic form gives k = 142.3 A·s^0.5/mm² and Smin = 75.4 mm². Energy balance with resistivity at the mean of 90 °C and 250 °C gives Smin = 75.9 mm². V70 fails both by 7 to 8%. V95 passes both by 25%. Voltage-drop approximations that drop the reactive term still leave every cable under 6 V against 12 V."
    },
    "reference_design": {
      "cable": "V95",
      "ampacity_A": 301,
      "voltage_drop_V": 2.98,
      "cost_EUR_per_m": 18.6
    },
    "worked_solution": "Ampacity and voltage drop use the catalogue. sin(arccos(0.85)) = 0.5268. R at 90 °C is the catalogue value. dV = sqrt(3)*180*(R*0.85+X*0.5268)*0.040 gives 5.19, 3.86, 2.98 and 2.47 V, all under 12 V. All ampacities exceed 180 A. Fault heating: rho20 = 1.724e-8 ohm·m, alpha = 0.00393 /K, beta = 1/alpha - 20 = 234.45 °C, Qc = 8890*385 = 3.42265e6 J/m³·K. k = sqrt(Qc*(beta+20)/rho20 * ln((beta+250)/(beta+90))) = 1.423e8 A/m² = 142.3 A·s^0.5/mm². I*sqrt(t) = 12000*sqrt(0.8) = 10733 A·s^0.5. Smin = 75.4 mm². End temperature from ln((beta+Tf)/(beta+90)) = (I²t)*rho20/(S²*Qc*(beta+20)). V50: Tf = 573 °C. V70: Tf = 282 °C, 13% over 250 °C. V95: Tf = 183 °C, 27% under 250 °C. V120: Tf = 146 °C, higher cost. Lowest-cost cable that also finishes the fault below 250 °C is V95. Matching ampacity and voltage drop only selects V50.",
    "wrong_designs": [
      {
        "values": {"cable": "V50", "ampacity_A": 196, "voltage_drop_V": 5.19, "cost_EUR_per_m": 9.2},
        "failed_requirement_ids": ["R3"],
        "why": "Cheapest cable that covers 180 A and the voltage-drop limit. A 12 kA fault cleared in 0.8 s ends at 573 °C, far above 250 °C."
      },
      {
        "values": {"cable": "V70", "ampacity_A": 246, "voltage_drop_V": 3.86, "cost_EUR_per_m": 13.4},
        "failed_requirement_ids": ["R3"],
        "why": "Next section still has adiabatic end temperature 282 °C, 13% above 250 °C."
      }
    ],
    "corpus_pages": [
      {
        "title": "Harton Cable Vanta copper singles, sheet HV-2",
        "markdown": "# Harton Cable — Vanta single-core copper\n\nInstalled in free air, 40 °C ambient. Ampacity is the continuous current for that arrangement. R and X are per conductor at 90 °C conductor temperature, trefoil.\n\nCopper: electrical resistivity at 20 °C is 1.724e-8 ohm·m. Resistance temperature coefficient is 0.00393 per kelvin from 20 °C. Density 8890 kg/m³. Specific heat 385 J/kg·K.\n\nInsulation temperature limits: 90 °C continuous, 250 °C short-time.\n\n| Cable | Section mm² | Ampacity A | R ohm/km | X ohm/km | Cost EUR/m |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| V50 | 50 | 196 | 0.4397 | 0.080 | 9.2 |\n| V70 | 70 | 246 | 0.3140 | 0.080 | 13.4 |\n| V95 | 95 | 301 | 0.2314 | 0.080 | 18.6 |\n| V120 | 120 | 352 | 0.1832 | 0.080 | 24.0 |"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "T4-54",
